{
 "slug": "bengaluru",
 "lines": [
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Almost every lake you see in Bengaluru was built by hand.",
   "chunks": [
    "ALMOST EVERY *LAKE*",
    "YOU SEE IN|*BENGALURU*",
    "WAS BUILT|*BY HAND.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Over 1,100 years. Then the city lost most of them.",
   "chunks": [
    "OVER *1,100 YEARS.*",
    "THEN THE CITY|LOST *MOST OF THEM.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "So why build lakes at all?",
   "chunks": [
    "SO WHY BUILD|*LAKES* AT ALL?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Look at the map. Bengaluru sits on a ridge, about 920 metres up.",
   "chunks": [
    "LOOK AT THE MAP.",
    "*BENGALURU* SITS|ON A *RIDGE,*",
    "ABOUT *920 METRES* UP."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "No big river flows here. Rivers run downhill. Bengaluru is the hill.",
   "chunks": [
    "NO BIG *RIVER*|FLOWS HERE.",
    "RIVERS RUN *DOWNHILL.*",
    "BENGALURU|*IS THE HILL.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "So how do you fill lakes, with no river?",
   "chunks": [
    "SO HOW DO YOU|FILL *LAKES,*",
    "WITH *NO RIVER?*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Rewind to the 800s.",
   "chunks": [
    "REWIND TO|THE *800s.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "People built earth walls across the valleys, to trap the rain.",
   "chunks": [
    "PEOPLE BUILT|*EARTH WALLS*",
    "ACROSS THE *VALLEYS,*",
    "TO TRAP|THE *RAIN.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Rain fills one lake. It spills into the next. Then the next.",
   "chunks": [
    "RAIN FILLS|*ONE LAKE.*",
    "IT *SPILLS*|INTO THE NEXT.",
    "THEN *THE NEXT.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Wheee! Lake number seven!",
   "chunks": [
    "*WHEEE!*",
    "LAKE NUMBER|*SEVEN!*"
   ],
   "speaker": "drop"
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Canals linked them into six chains, stepping down three valleys.",
   "chunks": [
    "*CANALS* LINKED THEM|INTO *SIX CHAINS,*",
    "STEPPING DOWN|*THREE VALLEYS.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "In 1537, Kempegowda founded the city, and kept building more.",
   "chunks": [
    "IN *1537,*",
    "*KEMPEGOWDA*|FOUNDED THE CITY,",
    "AND KEPT|BUILDING *MORE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Then the city grew. And grew. And grew.",
   "chunks": [
    "THEN THE CITY|*GREW.*",
    "AND *GREW.*",
    "AND *GREW.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "From 1973 to 2013, about 79% of its water bodies vanished.",
   "chunks": [
    "FROM *1973*|TO *2013,*",
    "ABOUT *79%*|OF ITS WATER BODIES",
    "*VANISHED.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "So today, water is pumped about 100 km from the Kaveri, and lifted 300 metres uphill.",
   "chunks": [
    "SO TODAY, WATER|IS *PUMPED*",
    "ABOUT *100 KM*|FROM THE *KAVERI,*",
    "AND LIFTED|*300 METRES* UPHILL."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "The city that built its own lakes now borrows a river.",
   "chunks": [
    "THE CITY THAT BUILT|ITS OWN *LAKES*",
    "NOW *BORROWS*|A *RIVER.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "And the lost lakes? Many are hiding in plain sight.",
   "chunks": [
    "AND THE|*LOST LAKES?*",
    "MANY ARE HIDING|IN *PLAIN SIGHT.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Kanteerava Stadium? Sampangi Lake.",
   "chunks": [
    "KANTEERAVA STADIUM?",
    "*SAMPANGI LAKE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "KR Market? Siddikatte Lake.",
   "chunks": [
    "KR MARKET?",
    "*SIDDIKATTE LAKE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Majestic bus stand? Dharmambudhi Lake.",
   "chunks": [
    "MAJESTIC BUS STAND?",
    "*DHARMAMBUDHI LAKE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Technically, I'm parked in a lake.",
   "chunks": [
    "*TECHNICALLY,*",
    "I'M PARKED|IN A *LAKE.*"
   ],
   "speaker": "bus"
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "Bengaluru never had a big river. So it made lakes instead.",
   "chunks": [
    "BENGALURU NEVER HAD|A BIG *RIVER.*",
    "SO IT MADE|*LAKES* INSTEAD."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 0,
   "text": "This is BHUGOL. Follow for more Geography Fun Facts.",
   "chunks": [
    "THIS IS *BHUGOL.*",
    "FOLLOW FOR MORE|GEOGRAPHY FUN FACTS."
   ]
  }
 ],
